00:41:48.873 --> 00:41:51.609
So I'm gonna talk
about Seth Stewart,

00:41:51.609 --> 00:41:53.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
the fellow that goes
around on Valentine's Day,

00:41:53.911 --> 00:41:55.646
and gives roses to people.

00:41:56.847 --> 00:41:59.083
The reason I picked him
is because, you know,

00:41:59.083 --> 00:42:02.820 align:start size:97% position:3%
a few years ago on February
14th, Valentine's Day,

00:42:02.820 --> 00:42:07.024
him and his buddies thought
to themselves, you know,

00:42:07.024 --> 00:42:10.060
Valentine's Day is important
for people that have, you know,

00:42:10.060 --> 00:42:13.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
a girlfriend or boyfriend
or significant other,

00:42:13.130 --> 00:42:14.798 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, they know that
they're gonna get something,

00:42:14.798 --> 00:42:16.567
but what about Valentine's Day

00:42:16.567 --> 00:42:20.538 align:start position:0%
for people who aren't expecting
a delivery at the door?

00:42:20.538 --> 00:42:24.308
So what he wanted to do
was give roses to people

00:42:24.308 --> 00:42:26.310
that don't have their
significant other,

00:42:26.310 --> 00:42:28.078
or a loved one in their life.

00:42:28.078 --> 00:42:31.248 align:start size:84% position:16%
So he prompted people
via social media

00:42:31.248 --> 00:42:34.018 align:start size:81% position:19%
to nominate people
to get a rose.

00:42:34.018 --> 00:42:37.054
And so he would go
to these, you know,

00:42:37.054 --> 00:42:40.291 align:start size:84% position:16%
these residences where
there were widows,

00:42:40.291 --> 00:42:43.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
or people who were having
a really tough time,

00:42:44.828 --> 00:42:48.832 align:start size:97% position:3%
and so this became sort of,
you know, a movement, I guess.

00:42:48.832 --> 00:42:50.634
And he was, every year,

00:42:50.634 --> 00:42:52.803
it was getting bigger
and bigger and bigger.

00:42:52.803 --> 00:42:55.573
And so when I talked to him,
he was such a wonderful guy.

00:42:55.573 --> 00:42:57.007
I love chatting with him,

00:42:57.007 --> 00:42:58.943
and he's just had this
great sense of humor,

00:42:58.943 --> 00:43:00.578 align:start size:84% position:16%
and, you know, I
asked him, I'm like,

00:43:00.578 --> 00:43:01.512
"So you have a girlfriend.

00:43:01.512 --> 00:43:02.980
"How does she feel about this?

00:43:02.980 --> 00:43:05.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You know, you go and
give roses to everybody."

00:43:05.149 --> 00:43:08.118 align:start size:97% position:3%
And he said, "Well, you
know, she thinks it's great."

00:43:08.118 --> 00:43:09.386
I said, "Well, of
course she does

00:43:09.386 --> 00:43:10.854
"because you're doing
something important."

00:43:10.854 --> 00:43:15.192 align:start position:0%
And his point was, "I'm not
giving roses to like, you know,

00:43:15.192 --> 00:43:17.194
"women who I wanna date,

00:43:17.194 --> 00:43:20.097 align:start position:0%
"I'm giving roses to people
who aren't expecting something,

00:43:20.097 --> 00:43:22.533 align:start size:97% position:3%
"that they've had some
kind of loss in their life,

00:43:22.533 --> 00:43:24.668
"or they have lost somebody,

00:43:24.668 --> 00:43:26.870 align:start size:84% position:16%
"and maybe they're
not having a good day,

00:43:26.870 --> 00:43:30.975 align:start size:97% position:3%
"and just a delivery of a rose
can change their outlook."

00:43:32.476 --> 00:43:37.314 align:start size:84% position:16%
And you can, you
know, he sent me notes

00:43:37.314 --> 00:43:38.949
that people wrote afterwards,

00:43:38.949 --> 00:43:42.319
about how important
that one gesture was.

00:43:42.319 --> 00:43:43.988
And then when I talked to Seth,

00:43:43.988 --> 00:43:45.990 align:start size:84% position:16%
he told me something
about himself.

00:43:45.990 --> 00:43:49.526 align:start size:84% position:16%
He too was diagnosed
with diabetes,

00:43:49.526 --> 00:43:53.263 align:start position:0%
and he talked about his
struggle and how, at one point,

00:43:53.263 --> 00:43:56.867
he got to the point where he
didn't wanna live anymore.

00:43:56.867 --> 00:44:00.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he told me this story,
and it just, you know,

00:44:00.037 --> 00:44:01.405
it made my heart break.

00:44:01.405 --> 00:44:04.108 align:start size:84% position:16%
But the point was
is that he's so glad

00:44:04.108 --> 00:44:09.079
that he wanted to stay alive
and do this for other people.

00:44:09.079 --> 00:44:13.083 align:start size:97% position:3%
And how it's important that
when we go through challenges,

00:44:13.083 --> 00:44:15.586
we realize that coming
out of those challenges,

00:44:15.586 --> 00:44:17.287
we can be better people.

00:44:17.287 --> 00:44:19.923
We can do things to
better ourselves,

00:44:19.923 --> 00:44:21.458
be better human beings,

00:44:21.458 --> 00:44:25.863 align:start size:88% position:13%
and so that just struck
me because I never
thought about him

00:44:25.863 --> 00:44:28.565 align:start size:84% position:16%
telling me this
backstory to his life,

00:44:28.565 --> 00:44:31.902
but it was important because
it kinda gives you an inside

00:44:31.902 --> 00:44:35.539
to where this guy is coming
from, where his heart is.

00:44:35.539 --> 00:44:38.275 align:start size:97% position:3%
And you know, his background
about how he really

00:44:38.275 --> 00:44:40.077
truly wants to do good things

00:44:40.077 --> 00:44:43.313
for other people to
change their day.

00:44:43.313 --> 00:44:45.783 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Well, Janice, I think your
story is basically proof

00:44:45.783 --> 00:44:47.384
that you're making
your own sunshine

00:44:47.384 --> 00:44:50.988 align:start size:81% position:19%
in a year that was
pretty bizarre.

